; claude: a software synthesizer, from scratch, for teaching digital
; audio and signal processing: one idea per module, each .mli with its
; diagram, worked example and references (see
; docs/claude_notes/plan_audio_teaching.md and notes_audio.md).
; Independent of the Playground (Audio.ml is the adapter).
; Private libraries, installed as part of elm_playground: pure OCaml,
; so every backend, the web one included, can use them.
;
; A library per subdirectory, each on the ones before it:
;  - signal/: the samples, and what's computed on them (Signal,
;    Resample, Mix, Spectrum);
;  - formats/: the files sounds and songs are kept in (WAV, MIDI, ABC
;    and solfege, MOD: plan_audio_formats.md), a library each;
;  - synthesis/: the building blocks of a sound (Oscillator, Noise, Fm,
;    Pluck, Envelope, Filter);
;  - here, the engine: a sound as a tree rendered ahead (Synth, Sfx,
;    Pitch_effect), tunes (Music), stereo and 3D (Space), the sounds
;    playing, pulled by the sound card (Mixer), and the interfaces of
;    what's played live (Instrument, Control);
;  - instruments/ and effects/: the live blocks of a synthesizer's voice,
;    and the live effects (plan_synth_teaching.md, notes_synth.md).
(library
 (name audio)
 (package elm_playground)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries audio_signal audio_synthesis audio_wav audio_midi audio_abc)
)
